@startuml Sequence_Booking_Request_Phase1

title Sequence Diagram - Phase 1: Request Booking\n(Temporary Lock Creation)

actor User
participant "API" as API
participant "AuthMiddleware" as Auth
participant "BookingController" as Controller
participant "BookingService" as Service
participant "User Model" as UserModel
participant "Vehicle Model" as VehicleModel
participant "Booking Model" as BookingModel
participant "BookingRequest\nModel" as RequestModel
database "MongoDB" as DB

User -> API: POST /api/v1/user/booking/request\n{vehicleId, startDate, endDate}
activate API

API -> Auth: authenticate(req, res, next)
activate Auth
Auth -> Auth: Extract & verify JWT token
Auth -> Auth: Decode userId & userRole
Auth --> API: req.userId = "698a71..."
deactivate Auth

API -> Controller: requestBooking(req, res)
activate Controller

Controller -> Controller: Extract userId from req
Controller -> Controller: Extract {vehicleId, startDate, endDate} from body

Controller -> Controller: Validate required fields

Controller -> Service: requestBooking(userId, vehicleId, startDate, endDate)
activate Service

Service -> UserModel: findById(userId)
activate UserModel
UserModel -> DB: Query User
activate DB
DB --> UserModel: User document
deactivate DB
UserModel --> Service: user
deactivate UserModel

Service -> VehicleModel: findById(vehicleId)
activate VehicleModel
VehicleModel -> DB: Query Vehicle
activate DB
DB --> VehicleModel: Vehicle document
deactivate DB
VehicleModel --> Service: vehicle
deactivate VehicleModel

Service -> BookingModel: findOne({vehicle, status IN [pending, confirmed], overlapping dates})
activate BookingModel
note right
    **Conflict Check Query:**
    {
      vehicle: vehicleId,
      status: {$in: ['pending', 'confirmed']},
      $or: [{
        startDate: {$lt: endDate},
        endDate: {$gt: startDate}
      }]
    }
end note
BookingModel -> DB: Query conflicts
activate DB
DB --> BookingModel: null (no conflicts)
deactivate DB
BookingModel --> Service: null
deactivate BookingModel

Service -> RequestModel: findOne({vehicle, status: active, not expired, overlapping})
activate RequestModel
note right
    Check for temporary locks
    by other users
end note
RequestModel -> DB: Query active requests
activate DB
DB --> RequestModel: null (no locks)
deactivate DB
RequestModel --> Service: null
deactivate RequestModel

Service -> Service: Calculate rental days
note right
    days = Math.ceil(
      (endDate - startDate) / (1000*60*60*24)
    )
end note

Service -> Service: Calculate price quote
note right: priceQuote = vehicle.pricePerDay × days

Service -> Service: Generate unique token
note right: crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex')

Service -> Service: Calculate expiration
note right: expiresAt = new Date(now + 15 * 60 * 1000)

Service -> RequestModel: create(BookingRequest)
activate RequestModel
RequestModel -> DB: Insert document
activate DB
note right
    **BookingRequest Document:**
    {
      requestToken: "abc123...",
      user: userId,
      vehicle: vehicleId,
      startDate, endDate,
      priceQuote: 160,
      expiresAt: "2026-02-10T04:45:00Z",
      status: "active"
    }
    
    **TTL Index on expiresAt:**
    Auto-deletes after expiration
end note
DB --> RequestModel: Saved with _id
deactivate DB
RequestModel --> Service: bookingRequest
deactivate RequestModel

Service --> Controller: {requestToken, priceQuote, days, vehicle, validUntil}
deactivate Service

Controller --> API: 200 OK
deactivate Controller
note right
    **Response:**
    {
      "success": true,
      "data": {
        "requestToken": "abc123...",
        "priceQuote": 160,
        "days": 4,
        "vehicle": {id, model, type, pricePerDay},
        "validUntil": "2026-02-10T04:45:00Z",
        "message": "Complete payment within 15 min"
      }
    }
end note

API --> User: Quote with Request Token
deactivate API

User -> User: Review quote\n(15-minute window)

note over User
    User has 15 minutes to:
    • Review quote details
    • Proceed to Phase 2 (confirm)
    • Or let request expire
end note

@enduml
